Well... That was weird.
It's a small game and a piece of art at the same time. It definitely does not try to please everyone.
My reaction to the general idea: wow, this game is like made just for me!
My first reaction while playing: this crap is boring.
My reaction after playing for half an hour: this is really enchanting, but this boring walking is killing me.
A final perspective: a cute, little game that could be better, but for a specific type of person is worth an hour of gameplay.
+ great idea, decently immersive;
+ stunning music;
+ unique graphics and cool animations of extremely slow world;
+ good writing and fascinating architecture;
- I hate walking simulators with little content, and you spend like 80% of this game walking around and wishing to have a power up to run faster or jump;
- after every restart the game crashed out on my PC, had to restart it every time;
- ... but seriously, walking isn't fun. Maybe in real world, but not in video games.
7/10

